# Elisha Bay — /storage/
#
# NOTHING IN HERE IS PUBLIC.
#
# This directory holds application state that happens to live on disk. Today
# that is storage/mail/*.eml — the complete text of every email the system has
# sent, including the recipient's name, their email address, their business
# details and the reference codes for their partner application.
#
# The directory listing was already refused (Options -Indexes at the server
# level), which is exactly what made this dangerous: it looked protected. A
# direct request for a filename returned 200 and the full message —
#
#     GET /elishabay/storage/mail/probe.eml   ->   200
#
# Verified before this file existed, and verified as 404 after.
#
# `Require all denied` rather than a RedirectMatch in the project root, because
# a rule that lives next to the data it protects travels with it: a future
# storage/exports/ or storage/backups/ is covered the moment it is created,
# with nobody having to remember to add a line somewhere else.

Require all denied

# Belt and braces for a server where .htaccess AllowOverride is narrowed and
# the directive above is ignored: nothing here should ever execute either.
<FilesMatch "\.(?i:php[0-9]?|phtml|phps|pht|phar|cgi|pl|py|sh)$">
    SetHandler None
</FilesMatch>

Options -ExecCGI -Includes -Indexes
